docs/plans/finals-rd-loop-2026-05-26.md:5:Build a tournament-mimicking benchmark grounded in real public competitor evidence, then run overnight R&D loops that take our bot from "passes a contaminated gauntlet" to "beats the strongest public bots by a decent margin under qualifier-shape conditions," so the 2026-06-01 Swiss qualifier outcome is a near-guarantee rather than a hope. Operative scoring metric: **cumulative chip delta** (engine README authoritative; "chip EV" is public-site shorthand).
docs/plans/finals-rd-loop-2026-05-26.md:11:- **Scoring metric**: cumulative chip delta. Engine README and `docs/tournament-spec.md:8,54-56` agree; the organiser-site "chip EV" copy is public-facing shorthand. Bot must prefer lower variance / ranking robustness over raw +EV all-in coinflips that hurt cutoff probability.
docs/plans/finals-rd-loop-2026-05-26.md:12:- **Adversary surface**: 5 behaviour-matched archetypes (`range_mc_pot_odds`, `blueprint_threshold_exploit`, `risk_gated_conservative`, `stage_variant_anti_punt`, `monte_carlo_basic`) **plus** cloned public bots Neel / Dominic / Famadeo / Vladimir / Saroop into `ext/public-bots/<name>/`. GitHub clones are not attributable to repo owners (only aggregate clone counts via Insights → Traffic; no usernames/IPs). Daily-cron monitoring was envisioned but triaged to a one-shot `git ls-remote` snapshot on 2026-05-31 (W2); the full launchd cron + watchlist alerts ship 2026-06-02 as part of finals prep.
docs/plans/finals-rd-loop-2026-05-26.md:16:  - **R2** — Field-beating: strict-positive 95% CI cumulative-chip-delta vs ≥ 85-90% of named public bots + archetypes; zero crashes/timeouts/illegal actions.
docs/plans/finals-rd-loop-2026-05-26.md:19:- **Elegance constraint**: each new module must (a) cite GT/math basis with `# Source: [[note-name]]` comment, (b) demonstrate measured benchmark gain, (c) survive a "delete and re-benchmark" ablation, (d) keep LBR exploit guard under the cap.
docs/plans/finals-rd-loop-2026-05-26.md:26:- Pre-X1 wins were partly driven by **name-triggered opponent-identity branches** in `bot.py` that pattern-matched on opponent string names. Commit `9904ed1` surgically deleted them (-67 LOC). Post-X1 honest numbers:
docs/plans/finals-rd-loop-2026-05-26.md:27:  - `template +71.82`, `mathematician +144.60`, `shark +69.81`, `ref_bot_2 +144.60` (essentially unchanged)
docs/plans/finals-rd-loop-2026-05-26.md:28:  - **`aggressor +176.03 → -236.59`** (`MANIFEST.md:79-80`) — the win was fabricated by the branch
docs/plans/finals-rd-loop-2026-05-26.md:31:  - H2H pre-vs-post: +0.00 BB/match, CI `[-3.36, +3.30]` → **EV-neutral when labels don't trigger** (`MANIFEST.md:87-89`)
