docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:33:- **Performance claim:** 15–17 chips/game vs **random**, 20+ chips/game vs **random** after mixed training, beats own checkpoint pool. Evidence is **screenshots only**. No LBR, no exploitability, no ACPC-style CIs, no human paired-seed match, no Pluribus comparison. Author's "beats pro poker players" claim is anecdotal, not benchmarked.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:38:### Explore B — Pre-trained 6-max NLHE weights landscape (May 2026)
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:43:- **OpenSpiel / RLCard:** algorithms only — only pretrained checkpoint is Leduc CFR, not 6-max NLHE.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:48:- **MIT-licensed compact 6-max preflop charts (Tyloo):** ~22 KB total, manually transcribable, but heuristic — not solver-grade.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:49:- **Verdict: NO drop-in solver-derived 6-max blueprint is shippable.** The only realistic external assets are heuristic preflop charts (already covered by our charted ranges).
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:53:- **No documented public-repo benchmark beats our numbers.** All four public repos (vladimir/dominic/famadeo/neel) ship benchmark harnesses but no saved score reports.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:54:- **Vladimir's `.streak/BUST_ANALYSIS.json`** records a bad run: vlad 0 wins, aggressor 60000 chips — evidence Vladimir loses to aggressor.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:55:- **All engine reference bots are byte-identical** (SHA-256 confirmed) between `ext/fullhouse-engine/bots/` and every public repo's copy. Confirmed source: Fullhouse-provided, not invented by any public repo.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:58:  - dominic: Blueprint + heuristic exploit overlay (`bots/dominic/bot.py:1`); benchmark harness omits ref_bot_2.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:61:- **Verdict:** We have NO public evidence ranking us anywhere in the field. We assume we're competitive based on our own internal numbers, which is reasonable given our internal benchmarks, but we cannot claim measured superiority.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:65:- **All 7 notes exist on disk, all 4–6 KB.** Shallow summaries, not deep research notes.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:68:  - **LBR (Lisý & Bowling 2017, arXiv:1612.07547)** — only inline references; no dedicated note despite `tools/exploit_check.py` depending on the concept.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:72:  - **Recent Deep CFR variants** (HDCFR, SD-CFR, knowledge-distillation Deep CFR, 2025/2026 discounted/predictive neural CFR).
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:74:- **Verdict: a focused /research run TONIGHT is worth doing, scoped to 4–5 narrow topics.** Top priorities by tournament-impact: (1) LBR, (2) Bayesian opp modeling for the 06-02 hand-history patch, (3) public-belief / range-conditioned equity, (4) action abstraction theory, (5) ICM.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:78:(Oracle synthesis — `untitled-chat-E35149`, captured 2026-05-27.)
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:81:- Vladimir's `gto_strategy.npz` (3.56 MiB, NumPy-only runtime, MIT): shippable in principle. **Skip in practice** — useless without his 274-feature extractor + 9-action abstraction. Adopting it = shipping his bot wholesale on 5 days. His Lane B win against us was INDETERMINATE (CI crosses 0). No.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:86:- Three unmeasured load-bearing assumptions: entrant count (Lane E used 128, real range 100–300), Swiss rounds (assumed 10, range 6–12), edge vs median entrant (sampled from 9 selection-biased data points).
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:87:- **P(top 64) realistic range: 40% (pessimistic: 250 entrants, edge ≈ 0) to 90% (optimistic: 128 entrants, edge ≈ +20).** Refuse to give a point estimate — that's the mistake Lane E made.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:92:- P(facing a v5-class ADVERSARIAL light-3-bettor) ≈ **25–40%** across 6 bracket matches — not 88%.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:96:- v5 was unreplicated, 1306 hands, CI half-width ~70 — actual loss could be −50 or −200.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:99:- **Step 3 (1h):** Regression bench `--six-max-mix` + LBR.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:105:- **Phase 2 (2–6h):** chained refinement — each result triggers a follow-up. Lane A leader → Lane A′ runs 5× more seeds on top 3. Lane B RED matchup → Lane B′ runs 10k more hands. Lane T −135 → Lane T′ paired-seed confirm.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:106:- **Phase 3 (6–9h):** commitment — long paired-seed validation of Phase-2 winners.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:109:### 6. Localhost leaderboard — <2h, stdlib only
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:113:- Reuse `_bootstrap_ci` from `tools/benchmark.py`. Emit JSON, then vanilla `<table>` with `data-sort` attribute on each header. Per-cell match count + CI width visible.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:126:There is no single root cause — this is a multi-thread synthesis. The dominant theme: **internal confidence has outpaced external evidence**. Lane E reported P(top 64)=99.94 % from a model anchored on unverified field-size + unverified Swiss-rounds + a 9-data-point edge sample. Lane B vladimir +55.30 was reported as a "win" but is an INDETERMINATE 1085-hand sample. The 9h overnight ran 1h not because of failure but because the queue had no Phase 2 / Phase 3.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:128:The single rule-relevant finding: `src/bot.py:39` reads `POKERBOT_DISABLE_OVERLAY`. Validator does NOT flag this (env-var reads are not on the forbidden-call list). Our INTERNAL `tools/audit_strategy_leakage.py` does. Strip the line before any qualifier upload; not a rules break, but a stylistic regression from the X1 patch hygiene policy.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:139:6. **CORPUS-RESEARCH-1** — Focused /research run for 5 missing notes (LBR, Bayesian opp modeling, public-belief equity, action abstraction, ICM). 4–6h off-critical-path.
docs/investigations/deep-investigation-2026-05-27.md:150:- Every benchmark number narrated as "win" or "loss" must include sample size + CI half-width.
