docs/plans/qualifier-finals-rollout-2026-05-27.md:239:- **Leaderboard tooling (A3) go/no-go** — **RESOLVED 2026-05-27T22:30Z (orchestrator): DROPPED.** Rationale: `docs/morning-promotion-checklist.md` §1 (Lane A acceptance gate) already enforces statistical sufficiency via three orthogonal mechanisms — aggregate bb/100 ≥ 1.5× pooled SE, per-template floor requiring ≥ 4/5 with CI low > 0, and catastrophic CI low < −20 disqualifier; §2 grades each per-opponent matchup by CI band (GREEN/AMBER/RED). The SHIP path (Section 8) carries the canonical artifact unchanged and does not need a leaderboard view; the MODIFY path (Section 7) routes through §1's gates first. Adding a leaderboard view would be inert in both paths.
docs/plans/qualifier-finals-rollout-2026-05-27.md:240:- **PATCH-2A statistical band** — **RESOLVED 2026-05-28 (user): pre-committed.** B8 must run ≥10 paired-seed bases × 100 matches each (~2.5h wall). Mirrors PATCH-1 reconcile rollup; rejects single-base seed-cluster bias. Acceptance rule unchanged: famadeo Δ ≥ +15 bb/100 with paired CI excluding 0, no public-bot HURTS, LBR aggregate Δ ≤ +20 mbb/g.
docs/plans/qualifier-finals-rollout-2026-05-27.md:241:- **PATCH-2B trigger thresholds**: C1 entry condition stated (Δ ≥ +15 bb/100, no regressions, ≤+10 mbb/g LBR creep, ≥6 h wall remaining). Confirm thresholds before B8 completes if you want a stricter bar.
docs/plans/qualifier-finals-rollout-2026-05-27.md:242:- **2026-06-02 hand-history release time**: The B9 5–6 h slot starts whenever the engine team publishes. If release is late-day, B7+B8 must run before histories arrive (PATCH-2A is structural and does not need them); B9 then runs single-threaded into 06-03.
docs/plans/qualifier-finals-rollout-2026-05-27.md:243:- **B4 sample-size sufficiency** — **RESOLVED 2026-05-28 (user): 50000 hands.** Upgraded from plan baseline (5k) to paired-seed-equivalent precision; ~10h overnight wall but A1+A2 are already GREEN so this consumes only Phase B head-start slack, not critical-path. Concentration verdict (top-2 explain >50%) is now robust to PATCH-1-reconcile-style seed-cluster noise.
