ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:3:> The UK's first quantitative poker bot competition — 1-5 June 2026, London
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:38:Open `http://localhost:5000` — you'll see 6 reference bots playing each other live with a real-time leaderboard and hand replay.
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:62:| `pot` | `int` | Total chips in the pot |
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:63:| `your_stack` | `int` | Your remaining chips |
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:87:- **768 MB RAM**, 0.5 CPU core per bot
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:100:- **No collusion.** If you and a friend both register, your bots must play independently. Coordinated soft-play, chip-dumping, or sharing live game state between submissions is grounds for both bots being DQ'd and forfeit of any prize.
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:101:- **No crypto-mining or resource abuse.** The 768 MB / 0.5 CPU limits will OOM-kill abusive bots, but doing it on purpose (e.g., to slow opponents) is bannable.
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:138:# single match, 400 hands (qualifier length)
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:139:python3 sandbox/match.py bots/mybot/bot.py bots/shark/bot.py --hands 400
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:149:**1 Jun — Online qualifier**
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:150:All bots play in a Swiss-system tournament (multiple rounds, 400 hands per match, 6-bot tables). Bots are paired by similar standing after each round. Ranking is by cumulative chip delta. **Top 64 advance** to the finals.
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:156:Top 64 play a single-elimination bracket live on stage. Winner takes the prize pool.
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:158:> **Why 400 hands?** Lower variance per match. With only 200 hands, "overbet a lot" can be +EV in tournament terms (you can lose −10k max but gain up to +50k, and only top 64 advance). 400 hands tilts the field back toward skill.
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:178:engine/         Game engine — NLHE rules, hand evaluation, chip tracking
ext/fullhouse-engine/README.md:199:**Fullhouse Hackathon** — 1 June 2026, London
